<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Second-Order SQLi - EliteHackLab</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.1/css/all.min.css">
</head>
<body>
  <div class="matrix-bg"></div>
  <nav class="main-nav">
    <div class="nav-brand"><span class="brand-icon">💀</span><span class="brand-text">Elite<span class="highlight">Hack</span>Lab</span></div>
    <div class="nav-links"><a href="/"><i class="fas fa-home"></i> Dashboard</a><a href="/labs/sqli"><i class="fas fa-flask"></i> SQLi Labs</a></div>
  </nav>
  <div class="lab-container">
    <div class="lab-header">
      <div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/labs/sqli">SQL Injection</a> / Second-Order</div>
      <h1>💉 Second-Order SQL Injection</h1>
      <div class="lab-info">
        <span class="lab-tag difficulty-hard">Hard</span>
        <span class="lab-tag points"><i class="fas fa-star"></i> 25 pts</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="lab-section">
      <h2><i class="fas fa-crosshairs"></i> Objective</h2>
      <p>In second-order SQL injection, the malicious payload is stored safely but gets used unsafely in a later query. Register a user with a malicious username, then trigger the injection when viewing the profile.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="lab-section">
      <h2><i class="fas fa-user-plus"></i> Step 1: Register User</h2>
      <div class="vulnerable-form">
        <label>Username (inject here):</label>
        <input type="text" id="regUsername" placeholder="admin' OR '1'='1' --" autocomplete="off">
        <label>Password:</label>
        <input type="password" id="regPassword" value="anything" autocomplete="off">
        <button onclick="registerUser()" class="btn">Register</button>
      </div>
      <div id="regResult" class="result-box" style="margin-top:1rem;"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="lab-section">
      <h2><i class="fas fa-user"></i> Step 2: View Profile (triggers injection)</h2>
      <div class="vulnerable-form">
        <label>Username to view:</label>
        <input type="text" id="viewUsername" placeholder="Enter the username you registered" autocomplete="off">
        <button onclick="viewProfile()" class="btn btn-blue">View Profile</button>
      </div>
      <div id="profileResult" class="result-box" style="margin-top:1rem;"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="lab-section">
      <h2><i class="fas fa-lightbulb"></i> How It Works</h2>
      <div class="code-block">
Step 1 - Registration (parameterized, safe):
INSERT INTO users (username, password) VALUES (?, ?)
→ Stores "admin' OR '1'='1' --" safely

Step 2 - Profile View (vulnerable):
user = SELECT * FROM users WHERE username = ?  // Safe lookup
messages = SELECT * FROM messages WHERE sender_id = 
  (SELECT id FROM users WHERE username = '${user.username}')  // VULNERABLE!

The stored username is used in a new query without sanitization!
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="flag-submit">
      <h3><i class="fas fa-flag"></i> Capture The Flag</h3>
      <form onsubmit="submitFlagInline('sqli-blind', 'flagInput_so', 'flagResult_so'); return false;" style="display:flex; gap:0.5rem; max-width:500px; margin:0 auto;">
        <input type="text" id="flagInput_so" placeholder="FLAG{...}" autocomplete="off">
        <button type="submit" class="btn">Submit</button>
      </form>
      <div id="flagResult_so" style="display:none; margin-top:1rem;"></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <script src="/js/main.js"></script>
  <script>
    async function registerUser() {
      const username = document.getElementById('regUsername').value;
      const password = document.getElementById('regPassword').value;
      const res = await fetch('/labs/sqli/second-order/register', {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
        body: JSON.stringify({ username, password })
      });
      const data = await res.json();
      document.getElementById('regResult').innerHTML = `<pre>${JSON.stringify(data, null, 2)}</pre>`;
    }
    async function viewProfile() {
      const username = document.getElementById('viewUsername').value;
      const res = await fetch(`/labs/sqli/second-order/profile?username=${encodeURIComponent(username)}`);
      const data = await res.json();
      document.getElementById('profileResult').innerHTML = `<pre>${JSON.stringify(data, null, 2)}</pre>`;
    }
  </script>
</body>
</html>
